# =============================================================================
# Line endings.
#
# `.prettierrc` sets `endOfLine: "lf"`, so `npm run format:check` fails on any
# file checked out with CRLF. Git's `core.autocrlf` setting is per-machine and
# defaults to `true` on Windows, which rewrites every text file to CRLF on
# checkout — so without this file, a Windows clone fails the format gate on
# files that are correctly formatted in the repository.
#
# Declaring it here makes the line ending a property of the repository rather
# than of each developer's git config.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text; binaries (images, archives) are
# detected and left untouched.
# =============================================================================

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicitly binary — never normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary

# Windows-only scripts must keep CRLF to run under cmd.exe and PowerShell.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
